<Page title="Privacy Policy — Sunalta" description="How Sunalta handles your alarm data, camera and NFC access, and support requests.">
  <main class="document" id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <a class="back-link" href="/">← Back to Sunalta</a>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="document-meta">Last updated: November 6, 2026</p>
    <p>Sunalta is free and open source. You can review the <a href="https://github.com/awaseem/sunalta">source code on GitHub</a>.</p>
    <p>Your alarms stay on your iPhone. Sunalta doesn’t require an account or include analytics, advertising, or tracking.</p>

    <h2>Your data</h2>
    <p>
      Your alarms, settings, saved NFC tag identifiers, and QR code values are stored on your device.
      We do not receive, sell, or share this data.
    </p>

    <h2>Camera and NFC access</h2>
    <p>
      Sunalta uses the camera to read QR codes and NFC access to read tags when you set up or stop an alarm.
      Scans are processed on your device. Camera images are not saved or uploaded.
    </p>

    <h2>Purchases and support</h2>
    <p>
      Optional tips are processed by Apple through the App Store. We do not receive your payment details.
      Apple handles purchase information under its <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you contact us for support, we receive the information you choose to share and use it to help with your request.
      Contacting us on X is also subject to X’s privacy practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
    <p>
      We’ll update this page if our privacy practices change.
      For questions about privacy, please <a href="/support/">get in touch</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Page>
